     ```java
     else if (Structure.class.isAssignableFrom(cls)) {
         Structure[] sarray = (Structure[])result;
         if (ByReference.class.isAssignableFrom(cls)) {
             // existing pointer‑array handling
         } else {
             // NEW: handling for inline structures
             for (int i=0;i < sarray.length;i++) {
                 if (sarray[i] == null) {
                     sarray[i] = newInstance(cls);
                     sarray[i].useMemory(memory,
                         offset + i * sarray[i].size());
                 }
                 sarray[i].read();
             }
         }
     }
     ```
     – The condition now matches any `Structure` component type, not just `ByReference`.  
     – For non‑`ByReference` structures, it creates missing instances, aligns each element to the proper memory offset, and invokes `read()` on each, thereby correctly populating nested structure arrays.

