- return null;
+ return "none";

So they added handling for NONE case, and changed default return from null to "none". The commit message says "Fixed minor bug which returns NPE when Checksum is None". NPE likely occurs because method returned null and later code used the string result, causing NPE. By returning "none" instead of null, they avoid NPE. Also added explicit case for NONE.

Thus changes align with commit message and indeed a bug fix.

