   – Only `firstSum[i] == 0` was checked before performing `firstSum[i] / secondSum[i]`.  
   – If `secondSum[i]` happened to be zero while `firstSum[i]` was non‑zero, the division would cause a runtime `ArithmeticException` (division by zero for doubles results in `Infinity`, but later `Utils.normalize(p)` could propagate NaNs/Infinity, which is undesired and considered a bug in this context).

